// ============================================================================
// PART 4: ARCHITECTURE DIAGRAM & COMPARISON NOTES
// ============================================================================
/*
 ARCHITECTURE DIAGRAMS:

 1. MVC (UIKit):
    View (UITableView/Controls) <---> TaskMVCViewController (State + Validation + Filtering) ---> Model (MVCTask)

 2. MVVM (SwiftUI):
    View (TaskMVVMView) <---> TaskViewModel (@Published State + Validation + Filtering) ---> Model (Task)

 COMPARISON (MVC vs. MVVM):
 - Testability:
   * MVC: Low — Validation and filtering are tightly coupled to UIViewController lifecycle.
   * MVVM: High — TaskViewModel has zero UI imports and can be directly unit-tested with XCTest.

 - Responsibility Boundaries:
   * MVC: Blurred — ViewController acts as layout manager, delegate/dataSource, state store, and validator.
   * MVVM: Strict — Model holds data, ViewModel handles business logic/state, View only renders UI.

 - Wiring Required:
   * MVC: Manual/Imperative — Requires addTarget selectors, delegates, and explicit tableView.reloadData().
   * MVVM: Declarative/Reactive — Uses @StateObject, @Published, and $ two-way bindings for automatic UI updates.
 */
